[s0l0!-header][h1]Handling Events[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Let's display an alert popup when the user clicks a specified button: [code format="html" codeId="962"]<button [b]onclick="show()"[/b]>Click Me</button>
<script>
function show() {
  alert("Hi there");
}
</script>[/code]
Event handlers can be assigned to elements.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="js" codeId="963"]var x = document.getElementById("demo");
x.onclick = function () {
  document.body.innerHTML = Date();
}[/code]
[note]You can attach events to almost all HTML elements.[/note]

